A||N||11||tesmith66||Modifying tach for V8||||1||
Z||000000||tesmith66||12-20-2001||09:03 AM||||How have you V8 guys modified your tach to work correctly?<P>------------------<BR>Timothy E. Smith<BR>1986 SE V6<BR>1984 Coupe||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||12-20-2001||10:24 AM||||I'm sure many people will respond with the various component swaps that can be made, but try this...<P>Find an 87 or 88 4 cylinder tach. Take the circuit board off and install it on your tach. <BR>Why?<BR>The four cylinder DIS actually fires each spark plug twice per revolution. <BR>I'm thinking (NOT completely sure) that this will work out to the same number of pulses per rev as a V-8. <BR>Anyone else ever tried this?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||12-24-2001||12:49 PM||||Yeesh. Nobody?||||reg||9
Z||000003||rockcrawl||12-24-2001||12:52 PM||||nope, won't work.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||voyagerspe||12-24-2001||07:03 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.thefieroclub.net/osg/tachmod.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.thefieroclub.net/osg/tachmod.html</A> <P>||||reg||14
Z||000005||Tina||12-25-2001||12:23 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raydar:<BR><B><BR>Find an 87 or 88 4 cylinder tach.<BR>I'm thinking (NOT completely sure) that this will work out to the same number of pulses per rev as a V-8. <BR>Anyone else ever tried this?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Second Rockcrawl here, didn't work for me.<BR>Myself, went for an Autometer gauges<P>I know  oliver@fieros.de  knows how to,<BR>he sent me the instructions once before.<BR>(Tossed mine after I got the Autometer gauges though.....making mental note here...<BR>Don't throw any fiero related stuff away  <B>Ever</B>)<P>Good Luck<P>Tina   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>This might be helpful too <A HREF="http://home.t-online.de/home/O_Scholz/fieroidx.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.t-online.de/home/O_Scholz/fieroidx.html</A> <P><p>[This message has been edited by Tina (edited 12-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||tesmith66||12-25-2001||09:23 AM||||Thanks to all for the input.<P><BR>Merry Christmas!!!<P>------------------<BR>Timothy E. Smith<BR>1986 SE V6<BR>1984 Coupe||||reg||1
Z||000007||rockcrawl||12-25-2001||12:27 PM||||If you go with the resistor mod as outlined on Olivers page <A HREF="http://home.t-online.de/home/O_Scholz/tach.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.t-online.de/home/O_Scholz/tach.html</A>  , the new calculated resistor value for a V8 is 210K. I used a trimpot and set it so the needle reading matched the scantool, and it turned out to be 208k.||||reg||1
Z||000008||jelly2m8||12-25-2001||02:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rockcrawl:<BR><B>If you go with the resistor mod as outlined on Olivers page <A HREF="http://home.t-online.de/home/O_Scholz/tach.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.t-online.de/home/O_Scholz/tach.html</A>  , the new calculated resistor value for a V8 is 210K. I used a trimpot and set it so the needle reading matched the scantool, and it turned out to be 208k.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Use this method, the capacitor for the V8 mod doesn't seem to exist.<P> When you use the trimpot like Rockcrawl suggested, you can adjust the tach perfectly. I mounted my trim pot remotely on top of the white housing for the guages, and all you need to do is remove the top trim off of the guage cluster, and adjust away.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||voyagerspe||12-26-2001||01:05 AM||||"Use this method, the capacitor for the V8 mod doesn't seem to exist"<P>Use 2 capacitors to equal the value.  you can add the values together to make the final value that you need.  I did this in my v8 formula works great the caps cost me a total of .95 cents.||||reg||1
Z||000010||GKDINC||12-26-2001||07:28 PM||||what is the value of the capacitor need to be  when doing a v-8 conversion. voyagerspe would you know the exact number?TIA||||reg||1
Z||000011||voyagerspe||12-26-2001||08:35 PM||||the value is 0.0064 uf<P>goto this site for more info <A HREF="http://www.gcstation.net/~mpupillo/tach.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.gcstation.net/~mpupillo/tach.htm</A> ||||reg||1
